{
  "abstract": "Using a 16-GeV linearly polarized photon beam, we have measured asymmetries in the process \u03b3N\u2192K+(\u039b+\u03a3) from hydrogen and deuterium, for square of four-momentum transfer, t, between -0.01 and -0.8 (GeV/c)2. The data show that for \u2212t\u22730.1 (GeV/c)2, the cross sections for \u03b3p\u2192K+\u039b, \u03b3p\u2192K+\u03a30, and \u03b3n\u2192K+\u03a3\u2212 are strongly dominated by natural-parity exchange, as is the case in single-pion photoproduction.",
